1
00:00:00,05 --> 00:00:03,02
- [Instructor] If you've never heard the term MERN before

2
00:00:03,02 --> 00:00:06,08
and aren't familiar with what it is this video is for you.

3
00:00:06,08 --> 00:00:09,02
Otherwise, feel free to skip it.

4
00:00:09,02 --> 00:00:13,02
MERN stands for Mongo, Express, React, and Node.

5
00:00:13,02 --> 00:00:15,09
It's a full-stack approach to building your frontend

6
00:00:15,09 --> 00:00:18,08
and backend with these tools and being able to build

7
00:00:18,08 --> 00:00:21,02
a full application end to end.

8
00:00:21,02 --> 00:00:25,02
Mongo is the database, a document based, non-SQL database

9
00:00:25,02 --> 00:00:28,07
that works well with JavaScript-based applications.

10
00:00:28,07 --> 00:00:33,03
A MongoDB database is one big object containing collections.

11
00:00:33,03 --> 00:00:36,03
Each collection could be like a contextual item,

12
00:00:36,03 --> 00:00:39,05
like for example, players for the database we'll create.

13
00:00:39,05 --> 00:00:42,00
Then inside the collection we have documents,

14
00:00:42,00 --> 00:00:44,00
which are the players themselves.

15
00:00:44,00 --> 00:00:46,02
So, one player would be in a document,

16
00:00:46,02 --> 00:00:49,00
another a second document, etcetera.

17
00:00:49,00 --> 00:00:51,05
And then inside each document we have the data

18
00:00:51,05 --> 00:00:54,06
for each players, such as a name, team,

19
00:00:54,06 --> 00:00:57,03
contact information, etcetera.

20
00:00:57,03 --> 00:01:00,01
The documents looks like adjacent object

21
00:01:00,01 --> 00:01:03,06
with a key value pair approach or arrays of data.

22
00:01:03,06 --> 00:01:05,09
Express is the web server part,

23
00:01:05,09 --> 00:01:09,05
and how we're able to build a Node-based backend.

24
00:01:09,05 --> 00:01:12,06
In other words, our frontend will interact with the backend

25
00:01:12,06 --> 00:01:15,06
through the use of Express syntax.

26
00:01:15,06 --> 00:01:19,01
React is the frontend and where we'll build the components

27
00:01:19,01 --> 00:01:21,04
that will allow our users to add players

28
00:01:21,04 --> 00:01:24,00
and see the list of players in the team.

29
00:01:24,00 --> 00:01:26,03
And finally, Node is the main element

30
00:01:26,03 --> 00:01:29,04
that allows all these pieces to fit together

31
00:01:29,04 --> 00:01:32,04
and is the server technology that is used.

32
00:01:32,04 --> 00:01:36,03
It allows Express to add its syntax on top of its server

33
00:01:36,03 --> 00:01:38,04
and create a web server.

34
00:01:38,04 --> 00:01:40,04
Although we won't go into a full-on course

35
00:01:40,04 --> 00:01:43,05
for each of these elements, we'll delve deep enough

36
00:01:43,05 --> 00:01:47,03
so we understand how each part interacts with each other

37
00:01:47,03 --> 00:01:49,02
and what are their functional roles

38
00:01:49,02 --> 00:01:51,07
as we build the soccer application.

39
00:01:51,07 --> 00:01:53,07
If you're curious and would like to learn more

40
00:01:53,07 --> 00:01:56,06
about each part, feel free to browse our library

41
00:01:56,06 --> 00:02:00,00
as we do have in-depth courses for each one.

